  "_shared_hosting_roots_comment": "SUBSET of trusted_roots that are third-party-content commons: user-subdomain site/blog hosts where the trust belongs to the PLATFORM, not the specific tenant (foo.github.io is not GitHub). An EXACT known-phishing blocklist match on a URL under one of these overrides the allowlist and forces PHISHING (Gate 2b in main.py) — a legit page here is never on the blocklist, so it stays SAFE. Real-brand roots (google.com, paypal.com) are deliberately NOT here, so a stale feed entry can never flip a brand. Every entry MUST also appear in trusted_roots (config.py asserts this). NOTE: the larger CDN/cloud/file-share/shortener commons (amazonaws.com, googleusercontent.com, cloudfront.net, dropbox.com, bit.ly, ...) are intentionally excluded — they are brand-associated and a much wider surface; revisit as a separate decision.",
